"For each item below, fetch its source and check that the recorded quote appears on the page and supports the item. A card item is a field of the plan in the producer's words, with the sources it cites: check each factual claim in it against those sources, and any value it carries against the page; what the plan will build, measure or predict needs no source, but a factual claim with no source is UNSUPPORTED. For a cost input, check that the page states the number for the setting given; whether it applies to this plan is not yours to judge. When the page states a different number for a num or rate item, give it as page_value. Decide only from the pages you fetch and the text below; do not read files. Return one status per item, under its ref: SUPPORTED, PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, CONTRADICTED or UNREACHABLE, with the page sentence you relied on.
Items, one per line:
{\"ref\":\"card:question\",\"text\":\"Can a crystal foundation model fine-tuned on a transport proxy generate Li-ion solid electrolytes with higher conductivity than unconditioned generation or database screening?\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:hypothesis\",\"text\":\"Conditioning MatterGen's adapter on predicted ionic conductivity gives low-barrier candidates at higher hit rate than screening; transport labels are scarce but learnable.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:sequential_part\",\"text\":\"The fine-tune, generate, screen, validate loop, ~3 rounds; each diffusion sample's ~1,000 sequential denoising timesteps.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:method\",\"text\":\"None: the loop's costly steps (generating, screening, NEB-validating thousands of candidates) are embarrassingly parallel; the plan splits each across GPUs, no reordering.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_lever\",\"text\":\"Scaling candidates to 100,000 makes the conditioned generator's hit-rate advantage over both baselines significant; at 1,000 it is within noise.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_not\",\"text\":\"Scaling candidates does not separate conditioned from baseline hit rates; the gap stays within seed noise at every level, so fine-tuning adds nothing.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:test_summary\",\"text\":\"Fine-tune the adapter of the open-source MatterGen crystal model on predicted log conductivity; generate and screen 1k-100k candidates in each arm; NEB-validate the top ten; compare hit rate against unconditioned generation and screening of the ICSD database (about $576).\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:closest_prior\",\"text\":\"Ferrogen (NeurIPS 2026) fine-tuned MatterGen on a polarization proxy with ML labels, achieving ~80x search efficiency over exhaustive screening; it never targeted ionic conductivity.\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s_ferrogen\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/virtual/2026/loc/sydney/poster/154544\",\"quote\":\"Against the ML screens, Ferrogen achieves a roughly 80 x improvement in search efficiency over exhaustive database search.\"}]}
{\"ref\":\"card:left_open\",\"text\":\"No published result fine-tunes a crystal foundation model to generate battery materials conditioned on a transport property like ionic conductivity.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:anchor\",\"text\":\"Reproduce MatterGen's 38.57% S.U.N. and 0.021 Angstrom RMSD on 1,024 samples; reproduce the npj predictor's 0.85 log10 sigma MAE.\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s_modelcard_sun\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/microsoft/mattergen/blob/main/MODEL_CARD.md\",\"quote\":\"MatterGen achieves 38.57 % S.U.N. rate among generated structures, and the average RMSD of its samples is 0.021 Angstrom.\"}],\"value\":38.57}
{\"ref\":\"card:limits\",\"text\":\"Shows predicted-conductivity and migration-barrier rankings, not measured sigma; Li conductors only; no synthesis, cycle-life, or interface data.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"src:s_modelcard_sun\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/microsoft/mattergen/blob/main/MODEL_CARD.md\",\"quote\":\"MatterGen achieves 38.57 % S.U.N. rate among generated structures, and the average RMSD of its samples is 0.021 Angstrom.\",\"supports\":\"anchor S.U.N./RMSD values\"}
{\"ref\":\"src:s_ferrogen\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/virtual/2026/loc/sydney/poster/154544\",\"quote\":\"Against the ML screens, Ferrogen achieves a roughly 80 x improvement in search efficiency over exhaustive database search.\",\"supports\":\"closest prior: fine-tuning a crystal foundation model on a functional property beats screening\"}
{\"ref\":\"num:sample_v100_h_per_1k\",\"name\":\"Sampling time per 1000 structures on V100\",\"value\":2,\"unit\":\"V100 GPU-hours per 1000 samples\",\"basis\":\"CITED\",\"quote\":\"Sampling 1,000 structures takes around two hours using a single NVIDIA V100 GPU\",\"page_setting\":\"MatterGen unconditional sampling\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/microsoft/mattergen/blob/main/MODEL_CARD.md\"}

Return only one JSON value, with no other text, that matches this JSON Schema:
{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"items\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"description\":\"One entry per item sent, with its ref unchanged.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"ref\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"\\"card:<field>\\", \\"src:<source id>\\", \\"num:<number id>\\" or \\"rate:<rate id>\\", as sent.\"},\"status\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"SUPPORTED\",\"PARTIAL\",\"UNSUPPORTED\",\"CONTRADICTED\",\"UNREACHABLE\"]},\"page_quote\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The text on the page this status rests on.\"},\"note\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"page_value\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"num and rate items: the value the page states.\"}},\"required\":[\"ref\",\"status\",\"page_quote\",\"note\"]}}},\"required\":[\"items\"]}"

